# brace-expansion 5.0.9 (CVE-2026-102276 and CVE-2026-102278, denial of service from a crafted
# pattern) sits only inside aws-cdk-lib's own tarball (node_modules/aws-cdk-lib/node_modules, a
# bundled dependency), so no lockfile change reaches it. aws-cdk-lib runs only at synth time on the
# build machine and is in none of the Lambda or agent bundles. aws-cdk-lib 2.273.0 bundles 5.0.12,
# which fixes both; npm lists it published 2026-10-08 20:05 UTC, so it clears the three-day minimum
# release age at 2026-10-11 20:05 UTC. Trivy reads exp: as midnight UTC and reports the finding again
# once that moment has passed, so these entries end at 2026-10-13 00:00 UTC and every scan from then
# on fails until packages/infra moves to that release. Ending a day earlier would leave under four
# hours, overnight in Europe, to land the bump before every scan turns red; this leaves all of
# 2026-10-12.
CVE-2026-102276 exp:2026-10-13
CVE-2026-102278 exp:2026-10-13
